  "notes": [
    "LAB-1156: a value printed on a fictional image, matched to the placeholder a contract-style text gave it in the same vault session; a false merge is a near-namesake's placeholder (eval/fixtures/visual/near-namesakes.json). Gold spans = values, tp = the image carries the text's placeholder, over_masked = false merges, mask latency = whole image masking per image (cached OCR).",
    "LAB-1211 re-run: letter-letter OCR confusions are real edits (except same-shape glyphs compared with case: capital I / small l, small e/c, u/v) and partial name matches need the card's tokens to be a subset of the session name (>= 2 tokens). The near-namesake set grew from 61 to 100 values (39 OCR-confusable namesakes: Iise Platzhalter, XJXK86KU4, LD8001464, ...). Before the fix, the extended set made the old matcher merge a namesake and fail closed (masking_failed); on the original set the numbers are unchanged (fuzzy 50/51 clean, 49/51 noisy, 0 false merges, 24/24 people consistent)."
  ],
